{"title":"Career Roadmap · NGO Program Officer","role":"NGO Program Officer","summary":"An NGO Program Officer plans, coordinates, implements, monitors, and reports on social or environmental programmes. With a BA in Environmental Studies / Ecology, the strongest pathway is toward environmental conservation, climate action, biodiversity, sustainability, community development, natural-resource management, and environmental education programmes.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 UG · 2026","Current degree":"BA (General / Honours) — Environmental Studies / Ecology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Environmental NGO intern, field/project assistant, research assistant, community programme intern"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Programme Associate/Officer in conservation, climate, sustainability or community-development programmes"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Programme Officer, Programme Manager, M&E Specialist or Environmental Project Manager"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Programme Director, Sustainability/Conservation Lead, Climate Programme Specialist or Development-Sector Leader"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Strong alignment, particularly for environmental and conservation NGOs."},{"type":"p","text":"A BA provides a useful interdisciplinary foundation, but competitive programme-officer positions increasingly value field experience, project management, monitoring & evaluation (M&E), data analysis, proposal writing, budgeting, stakeholder management, and environmental knowledge."},{"type":"h","text":"Best employability combination:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Environmental Studies","Ecology","Fieldwork","Project Management","M&E","Data","Grant/Proposal Writing","Community Engagement","GIS","AI Literacy"],"sep":"+"}]},{"he