ility"},{"text":"Environmental Economics"},{"text":"Environmental Sociology"},{"text":"Development Studies"},{"text":"Natural Resource Management"},{"text":"Environmental Governance"},{"text":"Environmental Education"},{"text":"Climate Adaptation"},{"text":"Conservation Social Science"},{"text":"Environmental Justice"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"The NGO sector will increasingly depend on measurable impact, climate adaptation, biodiversity finance, GIS, remote sensing, digital monitoring, community participation and data-driven programme design."},{"type":"p","text":"AI can assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Donor-report drafting"},{"text":"Survey analysis"},{"text":"Programme documentation"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"GIS analysis support"},{"text":"Literature reviews"},{"text":"Monitoring dashboards"},{"text":"Impact-report generation"},{"text":"Stakeholder communication"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But environmental programme leadership will continue to require field judgement, community trust, ethical decision-making, stakeholder relationships and understanding of local ecological and social contexts."},{"type":"p","text":"A strong long-term profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Ecology","Programme Management","M&E","Fieldwork","GIS","Data","Grant Writing","Community Engagement","Climate/Sustainability","AI"],"sep":"+"}]}]}